      "content": "that's a good start, but it's a bit too short. can you make it more intense? i want to really hammer home the idea that people who choose not to vote are actually hurting the community. like, make it clear that voting isn't just a 'choice' or a 'right' you can just ignore, but a heavy moral requirement. if you don't show up, you're basically letting the wrong people run everything and that's on you. can you expand on that? maybe add some language about how apathy is just as destructive as bad leadership.",
